<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Message (film, Moustapha Akkad)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1976</span><span class="sg-chain-h">used in the soundtrack, in the Hijra scene</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Medina (Maher Zain, album One)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2016</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sampled</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Grace and Gratitude (Olivia Newton-John)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2006</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung as an interlude</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Diriliş: Ertuğrul (Turkish series, season 1, episode 5)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Little Mosque on the Prairie (Canadian sitcom)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">closing credits, performed by Maryem Tollar</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Arrangement by Laura Hawley, sung by a children's choir in Ottawa</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2015</span><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Moonlight (Malek Jandali)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">piano and symphony piece using it</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Poemas Místicos do Oriente (Marcus Viana)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2003</span><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">My Muslim Family (Omar Esa)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2018</span><span class="sg-chain-h">performed in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">A. R. Ameen and Yuvan Shankar Raja</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2021</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung collectively</span></li></ul></section>
